<title>HONG KONG: HK debut 10-yr EF note avg accepted yield 7.57 pct.</title>
<headline>HK debut 10-yr EF note avg accepted yield 7.57 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Hong Kong government's HK$500 million debut 10-year Exchange Fund Note had an average accepted yield of 7.57 percent, the Hong Kong Monetary Authority (HKMA) said Monday.  </p>
<p>The average tender yield was 7.58 percent and the highest accepted yield was 7.58 percent.</p>
<p>The amount applied was HK$7.26 billion and the amount allotted was HK$500 million, the HKMA said.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843-6371</p>
</text>
